src/test/yb_subscription/README

Running the subscription TAP tests against YugabyteDB
=====================================================

This directory runs the upstream subscription/logical-replication TAP suite
(src/test/subscription) against an external cluster: a YugabyteDB subscriber,
and a publisher that is either PostgreSQL or another YugabyteDB.

Nothing under src/test/subscription is modified.  The harness is loaded through
PERL5OPT (-MSubscriptionCommon), which patches PostgreSQL::Test::Cluster->new()
to return an ExternalNode before the test body runs, so a test that says

    my $node = PostgreSQL::Test::Cluster->new('subscriber');

gets a handle to the existing cluster instead of one built by initdb.

What is in t/
-------------

Only the tests that needed real changes.  Everything else runs unmodified from
src/test/subscription/t, and run_subscription_tap.sh picks the copy here when
one exists.  So this directory is the answer to "what did YugabyteDB need?",
and each answer is one diff away:

    diff -u ../subscription/t/001_rep_changes.pl t/001_rep_changes.pl

200_* and 201_* have no upstream counterpart; they are YugabyteDB-only tests.

Running
-------

    ./run_subscription_tap.sh                       # whole suite
    ./run_subscription_tap.sh 001_rep_changes.pl    # one test

with PG_PUBLISHER_CONNSTR, PG_PUBLISHER_PSQL_PATH, YB_SUBSCRIBER_CONNSTR and
YB_YSQLSH_PATH exported.  run_subscription_tap_manual.sh does the same without
the environment checks, for driving the pieces by hand.

Subscriber flags
----------------

    yugabyted start --tserver_flags \
      'ysql_yb_enable_replication_commands=true,ysql_pg_conf_csv={yb_enable_pg_subscription=on,max_logical_replication_workers=6}'

The braces around ysql_pg_conf_csv are required.  Without them yugabyted does
not recognise the setting as its own, appends a second ysql_pg_conf_csv={...}
flag, and gflags keeps only the last occurrence - so the cluster starts cleanly
with the setting silently absent.  max_logical_replication_workers must be at
least 6: 010_truncate asks for that via append_conf, which cannot raise a
PGC_POSTMASTER setting on a running server, and without it the last
subscription never gets a tablesync worker and the test waits forever instead
of failing.  Neither setting can be changed at runtime; restart the cluster.

Extra flags for a YugabyteDB publisher
--------------------------------------

Running publisher-side as well as subscriber-side on YugabyteDB needs more,
and each of these fails in a way that looks like a hang rather than an error:

    --master_flags  'TEST_dcheck_for_missing_schema_packing=false'
    --tserver_flags 'ysql_yb_use_commit_time_ht_in_replication=true,
                     ysql_yb_default_replica_identity=DEFAULT,
                     TEST_dcheck_for_missing_schema_packing=false,
                     ysql_pg_conf_csv={...,
                       yb_default_replica_identity=DEFAULT,
                       yb_enable_replication_slot_exclusive_lock=on,
                       wal_sender_timeout=6s}'

ysql_yb_use_commit_time_ht_in_replication makes the protocol commit_time carry
the raw hybrid time; without it wait_for_catchup compares a hybrid time against
a PG-epoch timestamp and never converges.

yb_default_replica_identity must be set as the tserver gflag, not only in
ysql_pg_conf_csv.  It is read in two places (pg_create_table.cc, TODO(#22409)):
PostgreSQL's relcache reads the GUC and writes pg_class.relreplident, while the
DocDB table property comes from the gflag, and the master builds the CDC
stream's replica-identity map from the DocDB schema.  Set only the GUC and
pg_class reads 'd' while the stream still says CHANGE, so pgoutput rejects every
START_REPLICATION and the apply and tablesync workers restart forever.
pg_class is the one that lies here; do not use it to confirm the setting.

yb_enable_replication_slot_exclusive_lock lets tablesync workers drop their
temporary slots.  Without it each one dies at the end of COPY and
pg_subscription_rel never leaves 'f'/'i'.

wal_sender_timeout is not required, but wait_for_catchup waits for a hybrid time
read on the publisher after the last commit, which only a keepalive can satisfy.
Keepalives arrive every wal_sender_timeout/2, so the stock 60s costs ~30s per
wait; 6s cuts a full run several-fold.

TEST_dcheck_for_missing_schema_packing is a debug-build workaround for a CHECK
that fires when a table is created while a slot is being consumed (#32851).  It
is needed on the master as well as the tserver - the master crashes first, and a
tserver that then reads the CDC state table mid-outage takes itself down on a
second CHECK and leaves a slot row that re-crashes it on every later read.

Known gaps with a YugabyteDB publisher
--------------------------------------

Some upstream tests cannot pass and are not adapted, because the publisher-side
feature does not exist on YugabyteDB rather than because replication is wrong:
PREPARE TRANSACTION (021, 023, 029), CREATE/ALTER PUBLICATION ... SCHEMA (025,
028), ALTER TABLE ... REPLICA IDENTITY USING INDEX (031, #1124), a PRIMARY KEY
over some column types (002, 014), and non-UTF8 database encodings (005).

022_twophase_cascade and 100_bugs build extra local PostgreSQL nodes with
initdb, which YugabyteDB's initdb cannot do standalone, so they need a real
community PostgreSQL binary on PATH and do not run here.
